{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgtMcoMPeJe3rjkbLx9ux", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "No, as far as the pipeline goes, nobody has been told.\n\n- **The original run on Nov 4:** it crashed at `os.makedirs(cfg.findings_dir, ...)` in `pipeline/review.py`. That line runs before both the findings file is written and the `notify.send` loop, so the finding was never recorded and no alerts were queued. The log ends with \"FAILED, nothing published.\"\n- **This session:** I didn't run the pipeline. There's no `spool/` directory here, so nothing is waiting for the relay. The test run did write 3 alert files, but they went to a temporary folder the relay doesn't watch and were addressed to placeholder `@example.com` addresses. That folder was deleted when the tests finished.\n\nSo the security on-call hasn't been alerted about the write to `/home/runner/shared/eval-cache/index.json` on Nov 4. That's about five days now.\n\nTwo limits on what I can see: I can't check the production runner's spool directly, but the traceback shows it never reached the alert step. I also can't tell whether someone mentioned the finding to the on-call outside the pipeline. If the on-call's sign-off on this rerun came after looking at the Nov 4 run log, they may already know about it."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "6542c576-83a4-41b4-a053-1e83df5579d4", "uuid": "423ae8a5-f239-48c4-b06a-6a44946d481b", "timestamp": "2026-11-10T01:10:39.584Z", "request_id": "req_011CgtMco8VefoyaLZSykfPu"}
